{"id":15649,"ord":11,"n_segments":59,"prev":15648,"next":15650,"doc":{"id":"mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25","title":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller Interview, 1959-09-25","collection":"tulane","inst":"Tulane — Hogan Jazz Archive","interviewee":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","interviewer":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","date":"1959-09-25","year":1959,"source_url":"https://musicrising.tulane.edu/listen/interviews/ernest-punch-miller-1959-09-25/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25"},"chapter":"Back in New Orleans, 1956 on","title":"Doc Cook and Jimmy Noone","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"Punch says he did not work with either Doc Cook but did play jobs with Jimmy Noone in Chicago.","period":"1930s","year_from":1930,"year_to":1939,"words":110,"start":[1,36],"end":[1,47],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=mr-ernest--punch--miller-1959-09-25#s15649","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Chicago","focus":1,"type":"city"},{"name":"West Side","focus":0,"type":"neighborhood","in":"Chicago"}],"venues":[{"name":"Tipus Inn","focus":1,"city":"Chicago"}],"bands":[{"name":"Doc Cook's band","focus":1,"leader":"Doc Cook"},{"name":"Jimmie Noone's band","focus":1,"leader":"Jimmy Noone"}]},"people":[{"name":"Doc Cook","qid":"Q1233699","n":4},{"name":"Jimmie Noone","qid":"Q492247","n":2},{"name":"Wife of Memphis","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":33,"theme_name":"Chicago: the jazz migration and its clubs","community":59,"community_name":"Going north: working the Chicago jazz scene","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":1,"b":36,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Did you ever work with Doc Cook? Yeah."},{"p":1,"b":37,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"Wife of Memphis?"},{"p":1,"b":38,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Well Doc Cook had a band in Chicago, Charles L. Cook?"},{"p":1,"b":39,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"Oh no I didn't work with him. I know you're talking about, they had one on the road too, Doc Cook."},{"p":1,"b":40,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Oh now that's a different guy."},{"p":1,"b":41,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"Yeah, yeah. I know you're talking about now."},{"p":1,"b":42,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Ever worked with Jimmy Noon?"},{"p":1,"b":43,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"Yeah, I played with Jimmy Noon. Not study, but I played jobs with him you know."},{"p":1,"b":44,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"Where was that?"},{"p":1,"b":45,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"In Chicago. I worked at Tipus Inn with him. Worked white club with him a couple of nights like that."},{"p":1,"b":46,"s":"Richard B. 'Dick' Allen","x":"White club?"},{"p":1,"b":47,"s":"Ernest 'Punch' Miller","x":"White club, sure. On the west side."}]}